{
  "slug": "basketweave-throw",
  "title": "Basketweave throw",
  "subtitle": "Raised front and back post trebles weave a woven-looking surface.",
  "excerpt": "Alternating panels of front post and back post trebles build a basketweave texture on an aran-weight throw. The raised surface looks woven but is worked flat on a 5 mm hook.",
  "type": "PATTERN",
  "categorySlug": "crochet",
  "subCategorySlug": "homewares",
  "difficulty": "INTERMEDIATE",
  "sourceType": "SYNTHESISED",
  "sourceNotes": "Post-stitch basketweave derives from the raised-stitch family in Weldon's Practical Crochet (series 4, 1880s). Internet Archive.",
